stuffr ports parts of UnZip 6.0 to Rust: the decoders in stuffr-formats
(src/infozip/: crypt.c, inflate.c, explode.c, unshrink.c) and, in
stuffr-cli, the front end of its unzip compatibility family
(src/compat/unzip/: unzip, zipinfo, funzip). Two altered trees are
ported alongside Info-ZIP's own:

  - Apple's zip-33 changes to UnZip 6.0, which Apple distributes under the
    same Info-ZIP licence (zip-33's zip.plist: OpenSourceLicense Info-ZIP);
  - Debian's patch series for unzip 6.0, distributed under the same
    licence (debian/copyright of unzip 6.0-28ubuntu4.1).

This port is an altered version in the sense of clause 3 above, and is
marked as such: it is not Info-ZIP's source, it is not compiled from
Info-ZIP's source, and it is not an Info-ZIP release. The programs' banner
lines name stuffr and say "altered".
